            <ArticleTitle>Hepatic injury following feprazone therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>44-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases of feprazone-induced hepatic injury are reported. Both patients developed jaundice within one month of commencing therapy. Histological investigation showed a granulomatous reaction in one case and hepatitic changes in the other. The changes were similar to those seen as a complication of phenylbutazone therapy. When the administration of feprazone was discontinued both the clinical and biochemical changes were resolved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
